Bugs:
     [ ] When a project is booted, the `export_root` field in the `config.json` is not being updated with the value provided by the user during the boot process. This means that even if the user specifies a custom export directory, the project will continue to use the default export directory defined in the code. This issue needs to be fixed to ensure that the user's specified export directory is correctly saved and used for exporting encrypted files.
     [ ] The date provided by the software when you query project information contains too many spaces between month and day eg: Mon May  4 12:13:39 2026. Go figure.
     [ ] Do not create the `cipherlock_export` directory every time the project boots. Only create when encrypt/decrypt events happen. This will prevent unnecessary directories from being created and keep the project structure cleaner..

Cleanups:
     [ ] Make sure there is nothing left for TOTP.

CipherIgnore Templates:
     [ ] This is the same as .gitinore templates. Get as many as possible for multiple languages and frameworks. This will be used to ignore files that are not relevant to the project, such as build artifacts, logs, and temporary files.
     [ ] Create a .cipherignore file that can be used to specify patterns for files and directories to ignore when performing operations like encryption and decryption. This will help keep the project organized and prevent unnecessary files from being processed. 

